# Outcybers - Cursor Rules

## Project Overview

This is a Docusaurus-based website for cybersecurity education and services, focusing on secure coding practices and application security. The site is built with React, TypeScript, and Docusaurus 3.1.1.

## Technology Stack

- **Framework**: Docusaurus 3.1.1
- **Language**: TypeScript 5.3.3
- **Runtime**: Node.js >=18.12
- **Package Manager**: Yarn (preferred over npm)
- **Styling**: CSS Modules, Infima CSS framework
- **Icons**: FontAwesome 6.7.2
- **Search**: Algolia DocSearch
- **Analytics**: Google Tag Manager
- **Deployment**: Firebase Hosting

## Code Standards & Conventions

### TypeScript & React

- Use TypeScript for all components and pages
- Define interfaces for component props and data structures
- Use explicit JSX.Element return types for page components
- Prefer functional components with hooks over class components
- Use proper TypeScript annotations and type checking
- Import React explicitly in components that use JSX

### Component Structure

- Components should be in `/src/components/[ComponentName]/`
- Use `index.tsx` as the main component file
- Create separate `index.module.css` for component-specific styles
- Export components as default exports for pages, named exports for reusable components
- Use PascalCase for component names and file names

### Styling Guidelines

- Use CSS Modules for component-specific styles
- Leverage Infima CSS framework classes for layout and spacing
- Use CSS custom properties (variables) defined in `custom.css`
- Follow the established color scheme:
  - Primary: #ffba00 (yellow)
  - Primary dark: #e6a700
  - Text: #000 (black)
- Use Montserrat font family for text
- Implement responsive design with mobile-first approach

### File Organization

- Pages go in `/src/pages/`
- Components go in `/src/components/`
- Global styles in `/src/css/custom.css`
- Content directories: `/cheat-sheety/`, `/checklisty/`, `/clanky/`, `/kurzy/`, `/zranitelnosti/`, etc.
- Use `.tsx` for React components, `.mdx` for content pages

### Docusaurus Configuration

- Multiple content instances configured for different sections
- Czech language (cs) as default locale
- Algolia search integration
- Google Tag Manager analytics
- Custom navigation and footer configuration

## Development Guidelines

### Git & Commits

- Use Conventional Commits format
- Create feature branches with `feature/[alias-short-name]` pattern
- Prefer git rebase onto main instead of merge strategy
- Automatically commit changes when making improvements
- Amend to previous commit if it's a fix and the previous commit hasn't been pushed

### Code Quality

- Automatically add imports and remove unused ones
- Avoid syntax errors and ensure code compiles
- Write tests when fixing bugs to prevent regression
- Use English naming for variables, components, functions, and other code parts
- Create and use reusable components for clean composition

### Package Management

- Use Yarn as the preferred package manager (not npm)
- Run `yarn install` instead of `npm install`
- Use `yarn add` and `yarn remove` for dependency management
- Use `yarn build`, `yarn start`, etc. for scripts

### Content & SEO

- Use Czech language for all content
- Implement proper meta descriptions and titles
- Use semantic HTML structure
- Ensure proper heading hierarchy (h1, h2, h3, etc.)
- Optimize images and use appropriate formats

### Security & Privacy

- Avoid mentioning GDPR-sensitive information in tests, commit names, or code comments
- Anonymize sensitive data when needed
- Use temporary redirect HTTP codes instead of permanent ones for debugging
- When moving routes, create redirects from previous addresses for SEO

### UI/UX Standards

- Maintain high-quality UI/UX
- Follow the design used in the rest of the application
- Ensure visual consistency across components
- Use proper spacing and typography
- Implement accessible design patterns

### Monetary Values

- Use non-breaking spaces between currency and value
- Use non-breaking spaces within numbers when separating digits with spaces
- Format: "25 000 Kč" not "25000 Kč"

## Docusaurus-Specific Rules

### Content Management

- Use frontmatter in MDX files for metadata
- Leverage Docusaurus plugins for content organization
- Use sidebars for navigation structure
- Implement proper routing with `routeBasePath`

### Component Integration

- Use Docusaurus Layout component for page structure
- Leverage Docusaurus Link component for internal navigation
- Use theme components when available
- Implement proper SEO with title and description props

### Performance

- Optimize images and assets
- Use proper lazy loading for components
- Minimize bundle size
- Implement proper caching strategies

## Common Patterns

### Component Props Interface

```typescript
interface ComponentProps {
  bgLight?: boolean;
  // other props
}
```

### Page Component Structure

```typescript
import React, { JSX } from 'react';
import Layout from '@theme/Layout';

export default function PageName(): JSX.Element {
  return (
    <Layout title="Page Title" description="Page description">
      <main>
        {/* content */}
      </main>
    </Layout>
  );
}
```

### CSS Module Usage

```typescript
import styles from "./index.module.css";
import clsx from "clsx";

// Usage: clsx([styles.className, conditionalClass])
```

## Testing & Quality Assurance

- Write tests for bug fixes to prevent regression
- Ensure components render without errors
- Test responsive design on different screen sizes
- Validate accessibility standards
- Check for proper TypeScript compilation

## Deployment

- Use Firebase Hosting for deployment
- Ensure proper build process with `yarn build`
- Test deployment in staging environment
- Monitor performance and errors in production

## Documentation

- Do not proactively create documentation \*.md files unless requested
- Focus on code comments for complex logic
- Use TypeScript interfaces as documentation for data structures
- Maintain clear component and function naming for self-documenting code
